 "content_notes": "Tone: hard and dry; the irony is the captain who left before the boarding, never a joke about anyone harmed (no one was hurt). The headline case is settled: a seizure by the Irish Defence Forces and gardai and a guilty plea and sentence at the Special Criminal Court. The captain, Soheil Jelveh, pleaded guilty and was sentenced, and is widely named in the Irish press: he is named once, in the line that says he pleaded guilty, and drawn only as a dark rim-lit silhouette (NOT A LIKENESS). His fear for his family and 'captain in name only' are his defence's words, attributed as such; his family is never drawn or named. Not used: the cash amount (reports differ), Storm Agnes (one source), where aboard the cocaine was (the deck hatch is an illustrative device; no caption says 'in the hold'), the Hizbullah suspicion (an allegation), the other men's names. Rangers, crew, the detective and the barrister are generic figures with no badge, patch, flag, crest or insignia; the Rangers carry torches only; no weapon is drawn and no warning shot is shown. The ship and both helicopters are generic, with no name, number, flag or livery. The bales are dark wrapped blocks; no drugs are shown. Every card is our own typed graphic; no court document is imitated; no dialogue is invented. Facts verified 2026-10-25.",
